  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A liquid is heated at a constant rate in an open container. The temperature of the liquid rises by 0.50 °C per second until it boils. In a period of 10 minutes after reaching boiling point, half the mass of the liquid has vaporized.</p>\n<p>What is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\textit{specific heat capacity of the liquid}}{\\textit{specific latent heat of vaporization of the liquid}}\"></span>?<br/><br/></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{600}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{300}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{10}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{5}\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
